{
  "fixture": "gwg-pool-fiscal-year-fraction",
  "description": "A pool is dissolved in equal fiscal-year fractions, not pro rata temporis from the month of acquisition. Germany (§ 6 Abs. 2a EStG): the Sammelposten is dissolved in the fiscal year it is formed and the following four, by one fifth each — the first year is NOT shortened by the acquisition month, and the pool never reaches a sixth fiscal year. Until this fixture the core treated a pooled asset like ordinary linear depreciation: it laid out poolYears x 12 plan months starting in the month of acquisition, so an acquisition on 15 November 2026 wrote off 2/60 in fiscal 2026 (30.00 of 900.00) instead of 1/5 (180.00), and carried the last 10/60 into fiscal 2031 — a sixth year the statute does not have. Every existing pool fixture acquires on 1 January, where both models agree, which is why the defect survived. Whether the first year is shortened is a property of the pool regime, not mechanism, so it is declared per jurisdiction as poolProRataInFirstYear, next to poolYears and poolReducedOnDisposal (same reasoning as SPEC-004 and IMPL-019: a core that decides it puts a statute back into the substrate).",
  "covers": [
    "F-AST-001"
  ],
  "setup": {
    "tenant": {
      "name": "Fixture GmbH",
      "baseCurrency": "EUR"
    },
